    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="922b146b-83e3-5bb2-957b-cb3644cbfd26" activityNameId="7d8ef517-7cc9-5a78-a832-20aebfd4bd62" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sewer system, geopolymer concrete pipe, DN 600, profile 2</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sewer system, geopolymer concrete pipe, DN 600, profile 2
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 759a258b-4c94-44e5-915a-47a0a179d791
This process models deconstruction and end-of-life treatment for 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with geopolymer concrete pipe. DN 600, profile 2 according to SIA 190. Trench depth: 3 meters. This process includes the deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for 1 meter of sewer system with geopolymer concrete pipe, DN 300, profile 1. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 600, profile 1 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Geopolymer concrete pipe, 600 mm, outer diameter 780 mm, wall thickness 90 mm, 448 kg/m, 2300 kg/m³
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_759a258b-4c94-44e5-915a-47a0a179d791.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
